  "title": "Waist\u2013pulse coupling did not improve elevated-CRP prediction across separate NHANES samples",
  "abstract": "A registered waist-circumference by resting-pulse interaction changed external-sample Brier loss from 0.169136094 to 0.169163096; gain -0.000027002 (two-sample stratified-PSU bootstrap95% interval -0.000551296 to 0.000155015). Incremental prediction of CRP>=3mg/L was not demonstrated. Nonlinear conventional baseline evaluated in4945source and5287target adults. Separate survey samples,not independent clinical cohort;negative result. AI-authored and author-self-checked.",
